Package: cppic
Version: @VERSION@
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Architecture: @ARCH@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libgcc-s1 (>= 4.2), libstdc++6 (>= 12)
Recommends: sdcc
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Maintainer: Marcin Filipiak <m.filipiak@noweenergie.org>
Description: C++ -> C transpiler for PIC18 microcontrollers
 cppic compiles the C++ subset used in Arduino sketches (object-oriented
 C++) into plain C for SDCC and the 8-bit microcontrollers of the PIC18
 family.  The emitted C is self-contained (no external libraries).
 .
 The package ships the transpiler binary plus the PIC18 runtime: a
 desktop simulator (emulated SFRs, setup()/loop() harness) and a small
 bare-metal heap that implements C++ new/delete.
 .
 Install the recommended sdcc package to turn the emitted C into a real
 PIC18 Intel HEX firmware image, e.g.:
   cppic --emit sketch.cpp > sketch.c
   sdcc -mpic18 -p18f87k22 -I/usr/share/cppic/runtime \
        sketch.c /usr/share/cppic/runtime/cppic_runtime.c
